  <data name="UnihanTypeDescriptionZhuang" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The most customary Zhuang reading for this ideograph. Readings of words not part of the Standard Zhuang lexicon are suffixed by an asterisk.</value>
    <comment>Unicode Unihan database reading description</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="UnicodeTypeNameZhuang" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Zhuang</value>
    <comment>Name of the Zhuang script/language</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="UnihanTypeDescriptionFanqie" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A method commonly found in ancient Chinese dictionaries and rhyming books to specify the reading of an ideograph. The method uses two ideographs to specify a reading: the first one shares the same initial part, and the second one shares the same final part. For example, 德 (tək) and 紅 (ɣuŋ) are used to indicate the Middle Chinese reading of 東 (tuŋ), and therefore the Fanqie property value of U+6771 東 is the ideograph pair 德紅. The method uses a third and final ideograph, which can be either 反 or 切 (the two ideographs that correspond to Fanqie), and is therefore not included as part of the Fanqie property value.</value>
    <comment>Unicode Unihan database reading description</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="UnihanTypeNameFanqie" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Fanqie</value>
    <comment>Unicode Unihan database reading system name</comment>
  </data>
